    {
      "knowledge_id": "paper:din",
      "decision": "used",
      "rationale": "Target-conditioned local activation scoring is inherited, verified in archived v4 lines 250-277. DIN unnormalized intensity motivates no change here because local raw-magnitude AUC fell. Relative group allocation is separately tested.",
      "transformed_mechanism": "Inherited DIN-style target/key scoring; new local change is group-size-corrected relative mass, not DIN unnormalized activation.",
      "variant_names": [
        "density_target",
        "density_context",
        "equal_target",
        "equal_context"
      ],
      "nearest_work_difference": "For valid event i in occupied group g of size n_g, define w_i=softmax_valid(s_i-log(n_g)). Equivalently, first softmax within each group, then set group mass pi_g proportional to mean_{i in g} exp(s_i). Incumbent pi_g=1/K. Thus relative within-group weights are unchanged for fixed scores while inter-group relevance is restored without a size prior. Global attention pi_g proportional to sum exp(s_i) remains an existing utility comparison, not the proposed rule. For constant scores all occupied groups have equal mass; duplicating every event of a single group preserves the group distribution and summary; group score shifts now change group mass. Do not claim invariance to duplicating only a subset or all repeated exposures. All four standalone variants run the same allocations and differ only in evidence_mass and target_query. This is a parameter-free logit correction/hierarchical attention implementation; broader priority is unverified. Scoped paper searches for softmax/group returned no indexed match and are not an exhaustive novelty search.",
      "falsifier": "Failure to beat equal mass or query replacement leaves the corresponding utility/conditioning explanation unsupported.",
